Interview: Theoretical questions from all concepts learned till then including OOPS,DBMS, Computer networks, computer architecture etc

And questions from resume projects', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.32289,0.00000,0.00000,0.20179,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.60023,0.19447,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.30496,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.30012,0.00000,0.11979,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20053,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16433,0.00000,0.40072,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17809,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('032055f7779c8bca7af2adff6119992c9acfd7832c239dabdfe17fc1c9c49f34', 'Oceaneering', '', '2022-2026', 'IT', 'VEDIESH ANAND', '24 Sept 2026', 'Oceaneering International - Interview Experience', '{"Operating Systems","Core Mechanical"}', '{}', '', 'The process included a offline assessment, group discussion and personal interview ( combined core + HR)

Oceaneering was hiring for design engineer role. it reflected in their offline test. questions related to machine design, basic strength of materials. SFD and BMD , eccentric loading, drawing isometric view from given orthographic projections and subjective questions testing your design and optimising skills like designing a mechanism to lift the trailer of unloading truck without using the usual hydraulic mechanism.

My personal interview ran for 45 min approx. there were questions related to engineering drawings. difference bw first angle and third angle projection, why 2nd and 4th angle projection is not used.

situation based questions: if a beam is failing, what things u can do to make it safe. they made me draw bending moment diagrams. questions related to my internships. gave me problem and asked to design a mechanism for that application.

advice: interviewers sometimes ask questions to know your approach, not a perfect answer. you can answer in a way which reflects your perspective about the question. prepare every point on your resume, you should be able to explain the specifications of your projects and learnings from your internships.', '[0.00000,0.14327,0.00000,0.26488,0.11591,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08174,0.09633,0.00000,0.08775,0.10968,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09975,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.52494,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10274,0.00000,0.00000,0.11909,0.06723,0.10929,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12351,0.00000,0.00000,0.15321,0.08430,0.00000,0.00000,0.12101,0.00000,0.00000,0.17155,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12891,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12668,0.00000,0.00000,0.14105,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12560,0.00000,0.00000,0.09368,0.00000,0.07339,0.00000,0.00000,0.07845,0.11126,0.38258,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.32903,0.08502,0.11208,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09817,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13368,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13494,0.14968,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('860baf842131b17015f62143cbdc35dd6674bf6366c13a998074a1431f01f517', 'Honeywell', '', '2022-2026', 'CHE', 'JASLEEN KAUR', '24 Sept 2026', 'Honeywell - Internship to PPO', '{"Operating Systems","Core Chemical"}', '{"Be clear about your fundamentals and resume.","Know your projects well — understand not just what you did, but why you did it and what you learned.","For behavioral questions, use real examples from your college, projects, or extracurricular activities.","Most importantly, stay calm and communicate honestly. You don't need to know everything."}', '', 'Selection Process

The selection process started with the Online Assessment (OA) which consists of General Aptitude Questions and Chemical Engineering questions based on fundamental concepts.

After being shortlisted, I appeared for the interview, where I was asked questions related to my Chemical Engineering fundamentals, projects, internship interests, and behavioral situations.

A few things that helped me during the process:

- Be clear about your fundamentals and resume.

- Know your projects well — understand not just what you did, but why you did it and what you learned.

- For behavioral questions, use real examples from your college, projects, or extracurricular activities.

- Most importantly, stay calm and communicate honestly. You don''t need to know everything.

After successfully completing the selection process, I was offered an internship at Honeywell.

The Internship Journey:

I joined Honeywell as a Digital Chemical Engineering Intern and worked with the CCR Platforming technology team.

During my internship, I got exposure to tools such as Seeq and Power BI and worked on tasks involving:

- KPI and operational dashboards

- Data monitoring and quality checks

- Exception-based analysis and alerts

- Data analysis and visualization

- Supporting technology and performance reviews

One of the biggest learning experiences for me was working with real industrial data and understanding how data-driven tools can support decision-making in chemical engineering.

During the internship, I learned the importance of:

- Asking questions when you''re unsure

- Communicating your progress clearly

- Being open to feedback

- Learning from people around you

- Managing deadlines and priorities

I also realized that being technically capable is only one part of working in a professional environment. Communication, collaboration and willingness to learn matter just as much.

Towards the end of my internship, I got the opportunity to be considered for a full-time role at Honeywell.

I’m extremely happy to share that I have received a full-time conversion offer from Honeywell.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08095,0.00000,0.00000,0.05088,0.05995,0.00000,0.10923,0.00000,0.18423,0.00000,0.00000,0.08605,0.09061,0.00000,0.00000,0.06481,0.00000,0.00000,0.05778,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.32525,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19187,0.00000,0.00000,0.09594,0.00000,0.29650,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12066,0.08439,0.00000,0.00000,0.16563,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.45985,0.03559,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08735,0.14943,0.16047,0.00000,0.15003,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06950,0.05958,0.08399,0.00000,0.00000,0.09652,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18272,0.00000,0.00000,0.14648,0.00000,0.19844,0.16487,0.00000,0.00000,0.06826,0.05291,0.06976,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21893,0.08480,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07593,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09212,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15311,0.00000,0.07532,0.06269,0.09834,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18321,0.18527]');
