Before interview revise core Civil Engineering fundamentals. Specially of your internship

Know your projects and skills mentioned deeply

Give answers confidently in your interviews

Stay active will answering', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.25179,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.30061,0.16970,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.24467,0.34224,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.29256,0.00000,0.00000,0.26641,0.28868,0.00000,0.31976,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.32538,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.30301,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19801,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.24779,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('2ae67017b01d55a3a86f957603670f812c91a0ec8c1636c080858bb95b2acf54', 'Reliance', '', '2022-2026', '', 'HARPREET SINGH', '22 Sept 2026', 'Reliance Jio BP – Interview Experience', '{"Operating Systems","Core Mechanical"}', '{}', 'Know your resume thoroughly. Revise core Civil Engineering fundamentals. Prepare your internship and project work in detail.', 'Selection Process:

Online Assessment → GD → Technical Interview → HR Interview

Round 1: Online Assessment

Included core engineering, aptitude, reasoning, and general awareness. Questions were mainly conceptual with a focus on speed and accuracy.

Round 2: Group Discussion

Candidates were given a general topic. The panel evaluated communication, clarity of thought, logical points, listening, and teamwork.

Round 3: Technical Interview

Focused on resume, projects, internship, and core Civil Engineering concepts. Questions covered areas like Highway Engineering, Soil Mechanics, Surveying, Fluid Mechanics, and Construction Materials.

Round 4: HR Interview

Focused on self-introduction, strengths/weaknesses, hobbies, teamwork, career goals, and reasons for joining Jio-bp.

Tips for Juniors

Know your resume thoroughly.

Revise core Civil Engineering fundamentals.

Prepare your internship and project work in detail.

In GD, focus on quality points and active listening.

Give specific and honest examples in HR questions.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11603,0.00000,0.13278,0.00000,0.17188,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11871,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09289,0.00000,0.00000,0.08282,0.00000,0.26699,0.12395,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09166,0.00000,0.00000,0.42500,0.05998,0.00000,0.00000,0.21084,0.16028,0.00000,0.08648,0.24193,0.11019,0.00000,0.00000,0.13669,0.22562,0.00000,0.00000,0.10796,0.00000,0.18833,0.25508,0.00000,0.00000,0.11500,0.00000,0.00000,0.11500,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11302,0.13354,0.10341,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17081,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11206,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06548,0.00000,0.08384,0.06999,0.00000,0.17066,0.00000,0.12154,0.00000,0.00000,0.15169,0.00000,0.27035,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10460,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11815,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09927,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('d176cfc83f944316a882e2d175dcb69b531992d14ffb28634a12df10d0308a78', 'Reliance', '', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'ANJALI M J', '22 Sept 2026', 'Reliance Jio BP', '{"Operating Systems","Core Mechanical"}', '{}', 'Know your resume inside out — be ready to explain every project and internship in depth, not just what''s written on paper Connect your project work back to the job description explicitly (for Jio-bp GET: design basis, QA/QC, compliance, project coordination) — this shows the panel you understand what the role actually involves In the GD, focus on c', 'Selection Process:
Online Assessment → Group Discussion → Technical Interview → HR Interview

Round 1: Online Assessment
Covered basic core mechanical engineering questions along with general aptitude questions.

Round 2: Group Discussion
Groups of 10 candidates each, given a general topic. The panel was mainly evaluating clarity of thought, understanding of the topic, general knowledge, and ability to work as part of a team — rather than looking for aggressive dominance of the discussion.

Round 3: Technical Interview
A deep dive into the resume — the panel expected a thorough, detailed understanding of every project and internship listed, not just a surface-level summary. Technical questions were largely drawn from the projects themselves, and the round was as much about demonstrating genuine passion for the role as it was about technical correctness — being able to connect your project experience to why you''d be a good fit for the job mattered a lot.

Round 4: HR Interview
Centered on self-awareness — strengths and weaknesses, why Jio-bp specifically, and personal interests/hobbies outside academics.

Tips for Juniors:

Know your resume inside out — be ready to explain every project and internship in depth, not just what''s written on paper
Connect your project work back to the job description explicitly (for Jio-bp GET: design basis, QA/QC, compliance, project coordination) — this shows the panel you understand what the role actually involves
In the GD, focus on clear, well-reasoned points and genuine listening/collaboration rather than trying to talk the most
Be ready with honest, specific answers on strengths/weaknesses and hobbies — generic answers stand out for the wrong reasons
Brush up on core subjects (SOM, fluid mechanics, thermodynamics) and general aptitude, since the OA tests both', '[0.10431,0.10541,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19138,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14174,0.00000,0.00000,0.08069,0.00000,0.00000,0.09789,0.10171,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14679,0.10222,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09656,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22677,0.00000,0.00000,0.08762,0.04946,0.08041,0.00000,0.08694,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.39902,0.09087,0.09361,0.00000,0.22545,0.12404,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15531,0.16829,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17664,0.09484,0.08694,0.00000,0.10950,0.00000,0.00000,0.08528,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08216,0.14086,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05400,0.00000,0.34569,0.05772,0.00000,0.14074,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12510,0.16492,0.27869,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08626,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09700,0.00000,0.10889,0.19487,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08903,0.14822,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16372,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('b6a269fe941953fcae0eb095be275fb25bb723645c8d3665a2765290e3d409bc', 'Reliance', 'Graduate Engineer Trainee', '2022-2026', 'CE', 'RIDHI GUPTA', '22 Sept 2026', 'Reliance BP Mobility Limited', '{}', '{}', '', 'I was selected for the Graduate Engineer Trainee (GET) role at Reliance BP Mobility Ltd. (Jio-bp) through campus placements at NIT Jalandhar. My preparation focused on core Civil Engineering, EPC/project execution concepts, GD and HR preparation, along with thorough revision of my resume. I particularly revised RCC, concrete, foundations, BOQ, quantity estimation, construction practices, QA/QC and project management. I also prepared detailed explanations of my PWD internship, AutoCAD/estimation experience and technical project.

My key learning was the importance of knowing your resume thoroughly, understanding the job description and researching the company. I would advise juniors to strengthen their core subjects, prepare their projects and internships in depth, practise communicating their answers and remain honest when they don''t know something. Confidence, clarity, willingness to learn and genuine understanding are more valuable than simply memorising interview questions.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19795,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18681,0.00000,0.13094,0.00000,0.28141,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21741,0.00000,0.16799,0.09483,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12670,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11890,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14888,0.08066,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18183,0.00000,0.17000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.37711,0.17716,0.20208,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.39765,0.11065,0.00000,0.08994,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23984,0.15809,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15751,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18596,0.00000,0.00000,0.09340,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.28416,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('786bf7308a762948ef2f9f434a0a8138b9d296d32db43d2dc60a72042042705b', 'Mondelez International', '', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'PRINCE KUMAR', '22 Sept 2026', 'Mondelez International', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{"The Interview Process: What I Learned","Why did you do this project?","What exactly was your contribution?","What challenges did you face?"}', '', 'Getting a PPO at Mondelez International has been one of the most meaningful experiences of my college journey. What started with getting my internship opportunity in October last year eventually turned into a two-month summer internship from June to August this year, and finally into a Pre-Placement Offer.

Looking back, the biggest learning for me was that the journey was not just about getting the opportunity—it was about making the most of it once I got there.

1. The Interview Process: What I Learned

Before joining Mondelez, I went through the selection process, which itself taught me a lot.

Group Discussion

The Group Discussion was one of the first stages, and my biggest takeaway was confidence matters, but so does communication.

A few things that worked for me:

Try to speak early in the discussion if you have a relevant point.
If possible, initiate the discussion. It helps you establish your presence from the beginning.
Be confident and loud enough so that your point is clearly heard.
You don''t have to keep speaking continuously. Listen to what others are saying and contribute when you have something meaningful to add.
Whenever there is a pause in the discussion, enter confidently with your point.
Don''t be afraid of disagreement. You can disagree with someone''s point while still being respectful.
Most importantly, don''t speak just for the sake of speaking. Quality and clarity matter.

One thing I personally learned is that confidence does not mean dominating the discussion. It means being comfortable enough to put your thoughts forward.

2. The Interview

The interview taught me another important lesson: your resume is your responsibility.

Anything you write on your resume can become a question.

So, if you have mentioned a project, internship, technical skill, certification, achievement or extracurricular activity, make sure you genuinely understand it.

The interviewer may ask:

Why did you do this project?
What exactly was your contribution?
What challenges did you face?
What did you learn?
Why did you choose this particular approach?
What would you do differently?
How did you arrive at the results you mentioned?

They may also take the conversation in an unexpected direction or put you under pressure to see how you respond.

My biggest learning was:

Never lose your composure.

If you don''t know something, it is better to acknowledge it honestly than to try to bluff your way through it.

And throughout the interview, stay confident. Even when you are unsure about an answer, take a moment, think, and then respond.

3. Your Resume Matters More Than You Think

One of the most important things I would recommend to anyone preparing for placements is to make a strong and well-formatted resume.

It doesn''t have to be overloaded with information.

Instead:

Keep the formatting clean and professional.
Highlight your important projects and experiences.
Quantify your work wherever possible.
Keep your points concise.
Make sure every statement is something you can explain.
Proofread it multiple times.
Prepare questions based on every major point on your resume.

A good resume doesn''t just get you shortlisted—it also becomes the foundation for your interview.

My Internship Journey at Mondelez

I got my internship opportunity in October last year, and I joined the summer internship from June to August this year.

This was my first experience working in a manufacturing plant, and honestly, the initial days were challenging.

There was a completely new environment to understand—the plant, processes, people, machines, terminology and the way work actually happens on the shop floor.

Initially, it can feel overwhelming.

But that''s where one of my biggest learnings came in:

Trust the process.

You don''t have to understand everything on Day 1.

Take it step by step.

Learn something new every day.

Ask questions, Observe, Make mistakes, Learn from them. And slowly, things start making sense.

One thing I would strongly recommend to anyone joining an internship—especially a manufacturing internship—is:

Don''t stay limited to your project.

Go out and explore the plant.

Interact with people.

Talk to operators, engineers, supervisors, managers and everyone around you.

Because everyone has something to teach you.

Some of the most valuable things I learned during my internship came from conversations and observations that weren''t necessarily part of my formal project.

Don''t hesitate to ask questions just because you think they might sound basic.

A question that seems basic to you might actually help you understand the entire process better.

Understand Your Project Properly

Once you are assigned your project, spend enough time understanding why the project exists in the first place.

Don''t immediately jump into finding solutions.

First understand:

What is the problem? → Why does it matter? → What is causing it? → What data do I have? → What can I actually improve?

Ask as many questions as you need.

Take help whenever you feel stuck.

Talk to your mentor.

Talk to your guide.

Talk to people working on the process.

There is absolutely no harm in asking for help.

In fact, I believe that knowing when to ask for help is itself an important professional skill.

Keep Learning Outside Your Project Too

An internship is not only about completing the project assigned to you.

It is also an opportunity to explore.

So while working seriously, make sure you also take some time to:

Explore different areas of the organization.
Learn about processes outside your project.
Interact with new people.
Develop new skills.
Explore things you''re genuinely interested in.
Spend time doing things that make you happy.

Maintaining a balance helped me enjoy the experience much more.

My Biggest Learning

If I had to summarize my entire internship experience in one message, it would be:

Have fun.

Take your work seriously, but don''t forget to enjoy the journey.

Enjoy the problems you are solving.

Enjoy the people you meet.

Enjoy learning something new.

Enjoy stepping outside your comfort zone.

And enjoy the small wins along the way.

Because when you genuinely enjoy what you''re doing, you don''t constantly keep checking how much time is left.

And before you realize it, the internship is over, you''ve grown tremendously, and you''ve achieved what you were working towards.

For me, the journey from getting the internship opportunity in October, joining the plant in June, navigating the challenges of my first manufacturing experience, learning from the people around me, and eventually receiving a PPO from Mondelez International has been incredibly rewarding.

The PPO is definitely a milestone I''m proud of.

But more than the offer itself, I''m grateful for everything the journey taught me.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.03866,0.03383,0.00000,0.00000,0.04344,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.02561,0.06403,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.04249,0.00000,0.00000,0.03039,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.03813,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22495,0.03651,0.17993,0.44991,0.00000,0.00000,0.07850,0.03190,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.03714,0.07767,0.08944,0.00000,0.00000,0.13533,0.00000,0.00000,0.40050,0.08346,0.03050,0.00000,0.00000,0.24578,0.14016,0.03763,0.00000,0.21108,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.24703,0.00000,0.07008,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19694,0.00000,0.03124,0.13579,0.00000,0.00000,0.03666,0.00000,0.04117,0.02735,0.03920,0.10711,0.00000,0.27429,0.02290,0.06495,0.07445,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14889,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.03422,0.03977,0.02865,0.00000,0.03029,0.00000,0.03561,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.01933,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14361,0.00000,0.21193,0.02940,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.04344,0.09743,0.04296,0.17377]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('c277dcbfd9bb337e923fdde26f5787f316a7ff9316a423ea19502bb18abea969', 'General', '', '2022-2026', '', 'NEELI SAI PRASAD', '21 Sept 2026', 'General Interview Experience', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'My Gladify placement experience was one of the important learning experiences of my final year at NIT Jalandhar. Before the placement process, I prepared myself by researching about the company and the role, revising common HR and interview questions, improving my communication skills, and practicing how to confidently introduce myself and explain my strengths, weaknesses, academic background, and career goals. During the selection process, I went through the different rounds conducted by Gladify, where I was evaluated mainly on my communication skills, confidence, attitude, problem-solving ability, and suitability for the role. The interview questions also helped me understand how important it is to remain calm and communicate my thoughts clearly rather than simply memorizing answers. Each round gave me a different learning experience and helped me improve my confidence. After successfully completing the selection rounds, I was selected by Gladify for an opportunity in Jaipur. The offered salary was ₹17,000 per month for the first four months. Overall, the Gladify placement journey, from preparation to the final selection, taught me how to approach a professional recruitment process, prepare strategically, handle interview pressure, communicate effectively, and present myself confidently in front of recruiters.', '[0.13345,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10910,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12080,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13703,0.00000,0.00000,0.19601,0.12466,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23545,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18984,0.10287,0.21099,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12762,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07935,0.00000,0.21820,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21530,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13210,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22689,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10910,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12701,0.09512,0.30217,0.00000,0.00000,0.12582,0.11822,0.13485,0.00000,0.08818,0.00000,0.20724,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12004,0.00000,0.00000,0.14421,0.00000,0.00000,0.21099,0.07131,0.20501,0.00000,0.10511,0.33109,0.00000,0.18480,0.00000,0.09768,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11390,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14009,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
