Overall, the process focused more on quantitative ability, logical thinking, decision-making and personality than on prior finance knowledge.', '[0.40506,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13760,0.18333,0.12534,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19846,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14676,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19207,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12831,0.00000,0.00000,0.19368,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12041,0.00000,0.16557,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.24505,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16879,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21381,0.16557,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15952,0.13674,0.00000,0.14436,0.30572,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20968,0.00000,0.00000,0.11206,0.00000,0.36434,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12144,0.16010,0.00000,0.15556,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('611b1746ca43cdfb818dc27f8945487de5169318bc748b00a52abaac03615b41', 'General', 'Operations Manager', '2022-2026', 'MBA', 'HARSHIT RULANIYAN', '20 Sept 2026', 'General Interview Experience', '{}', '{}', '', 'My industry experience spans operations, product support and project execution. At Dreamcast, I worked in Operations/Product Support, gaining exposure to digital operations, workflow management, communication and cross-functional coordination. Currently, as an EPC Project Intern at Desire Energy Solutions Pvt. Ltd., Jaipur, I am gaining practical exposure to project execution, coordination and engineering workflows. These experiences have strengthened my problem-solving, communication, teamwork and adaptability while helping me understand the intersection of engineering, business and management.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.38572,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.44118,0.24905,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.25113,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10592,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23668,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17352,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.52216,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19221,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22414,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.27261,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('5f9612d8df262b0bb5a3279b07c3e45a1d4aeada2def581f54dc4e77f4a51ab7', 'Increff', '', '2022-2026', 'CSE', 'LUSON BASUMATARY', '20 Sept 2026', 'Increff - SDE', '{"DSA","Operating Systems","OOPs"}', '{}', 'Second tip: keep your internet off in machine coding round.', 'Round 1: PI Cognitive assessment, 50 aptitude questions in 12 minutes.

Round 2: OA(100 Core CSE, debugging and code completion questions in 1:30 - 2 hrs)

Round 3: Machine Coding Round + Interview - Implementation of a room booking system using Object Oriented Programming. Interview is mostly focused on your implementation of the system.

Round 4: AI Coding Round + Interview - Implement the same system with frontend and backend using AI tools and co pilot. This interview would be more focused towards your resume and core CS. Questions may include, Semaphores, Mutex, Paging and Segmentation in OS, Different types of Data Structures(Trees are imp), Information Security concepts like hashing, encryption, asymetric cipers etc.

Round 5: HR interview - Situational questions.

Tips: Focus more on development frameworks. Try to properly implement the 4-5 major tasks of the provided system in machine coding round and do not complicate the system. Make sure you can explain it to the interviewer.

Second tip: keep your internet off in machine coding round.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.21671,0.00000,0.00000,0.10980,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08133,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11789,0.37440,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07838,0.00000,0.16844,0.00000,0.11730,0.11030,0.00000,0.00000,0.12710,0.00000,0.10559,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09227,0.00000,0.09976,0.15168,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07117,0.24065,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.24139,0.08821,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10695,0.00000,0.00000,0.11909,0.00000,0.00000,0.11080,0.09428,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12784,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21534,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07178,0.00000,0.57564,0.00000,0.11030,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.25274,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('5fd19270a26d9aa2938f173f785aeedcce3c38b4bf8aba4b15dc5b4106001624', 'SRF', '', '2022-2026', '', 'ADITYA PAREWA', '20 Sept 2026', 'SRF Placement Experience', '{"Operating Systems","Core Mechanical"}', '{"Campus Technical Interview","Manufacturing Processes","Strength of Materials","Refrigeration and Air Conditioning"}', '', 'I recently went through the placement process for SRF Limited for the Senior Executive position. The selection process was quite comprehensive and consisted of five interview rounds—two rounds during the campus placement process and three rounds at Gurugram.

Selection Process

Campus Selection

1. Technical Interview

2. HR Interview

Gurugram Selection

3. HR Interview

4. Technical Interview

5. CEO Interview

---

1. Campus Technical Interview

The first round was a Technical Interview conducted during the campus placement process.

The discussion mainly focused on my Mechanical Engineering fundamentals, projects, internship experience and practical understanding of engineering concepts.

I prepared topics from:

- Thermodynamics

- Heat Transfer

- Fluid Mechanics

- IC Engines

- Manufacturing Processes

- Strength of Materials

- Refrigeration and Air Conditioning

- Basic Mechanical Engineering

The interview was not restricted to direct theoretical questions. Several concepts required me to explain their practical applications and reasoning.

Project Discussion

My projects were also an important part of the discussion, particularly my CFD project.

I prepared to explain the complete project, including:

- Problem statement

- Objective

- Turbulence model

- Reynolds number

- Nusselt number

- Validation

- Results

- Practical application

One of the most important lessons from this round was:

«Whatever you mention on your resume, make sure you can explain it in depth.»

A small point mentioned in a project can lead to multiple follow-up questions.

---

2. Campus HR Interview

The second campus round was the HR Interview.

The focus shifted from purely technical knowledge to my personality, communication skills, career goals and suitability for the organization.

The discussion included questions around:

- Tell me about yourself.

- Why SRF?

- Why do you want to join the company?

- What are your strengths?

- What is your weakness?

- Where do you see yourself in five years?

- Tell me about your internship.

- Tell me about your projects.

- How do you handle pressure?

- How do you handle conflicts?

- How would you respond if your manager rejected your leave application?

- Are you comfortable with relocation?

- What are your expectations from your first job?

The main focus was on giving genuine and structured answers rather than highly rehearsed responses.

After completing the two campus rounds, I was shortlisted for the next stage at Gurugram.

---

3. Gurugram HR Interview

The first round at Gurugram was another HR Interview.

Although I had already faced an HR round on campus, this interaction was more detailed. The discussion focused on my overall personality, motivation, career expectations and ability to adapt to a professional and industrial environment.

Topics included:

- Academic background

- Internship experience

- Projects

- Why SRF?

- Career aspirations

- Strengths and weaknesses

- Teamwork

- Leadership

- Handling pressure

- Conflict management

- Relocation

- Workplace situations

- Expectations from the organization

---

4. Gurugram Technical Interview

The second Gurugram round was the Technical Interview.

This was one of the most detailed rounds of the entire process. The discussion covered core Mechanical Engineering concepts along with my projects and internship experience.

Thermodynamics

Heat Transfer

- Heat exchangers

Fluid Mechanics

- Cavitation

- Causes of cavitation

- Methods to reduce cavitation

IC Engines

I also revised:

- SI and CI engines

- Four-stroke and two-stroke engines

Projects and Internship

The interviewer also went into detail about my projects and internship.

For my internship, I focused on explaining:

- What work I performed

- What I learned

- How the system/process worked

- Problems I encountered

- How I applied engineering concepts

- What practical exposure I gained

The biggest lesson from this round was that conceptual clarity is much more useful than memorizing answers.

---

5. Final CEO Interview

The final round at Gurugram was the CEO Interview.

This was probably the most different round compared with the technical interview.

The discussion was more focused on my personality, values, decision-making, career aspirations, motivation and approach toward professional situations.

The discussion included areas such as:

- Why SRF?

- What do you know about SRF?

- Why should SRF hire you?

- What are your career goals?

- What values are important to you?

- What are your strengths?

- How do you handle failure?

- How do you handle pressure?

- How would you deal with disagreement with a senior?

- What would you do if you were given a difficult or unfamiliar task?

- What do you expect from your organization?

- Questions related to my projects and internship

---

Overall Experience

The complete SRF selection process consisted of:

Campus

→ Technical Interview

→ HR Interview

Gurugram

→ HR Interview

→ Technical Interview

→ CEO Interview

Total: 5 Interview Rounds

Going through all five rounds gave me exposure to different styles of interviews—from technical fundamentals and project discussions to HR conversations and senior-management interaction.

Key Takeaways

1. Know your resume inside out

Every project, skill, internship and technical term mentioned on the resume can become a potential interview question.

2. Focus on fundamentals

For Mechanical Engineering candidates, I found it extremely useful to revise:

Thermodynamics + Heat Transfer + Fluid Mechanics + Manufacturing + IC Engines + Basic Mechanical Engineering

3. Understand your projects

Don''t simply memorize the project description.

Be prepared to explain:

Problem → Objective → Methodology → Tools → Results → Challenges → Validation → Application

4. Research the company

Before the interview, understand SRF''s businesses, products, manufacturing operations, values and the responsibilities associated with the Senior Executive role.

5. Prepare for situational questions

Questions involving managers, teamwork, pressure, conflicts, responsibility and decision-making can be just as important as technical questions.

---', '[0.03867,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.03161,0.00000,0.00000,0.04059,0.00000,0.00000,0.03501,0.00000,0.05983,0.00000,0.34450,0.03629,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.02840,0.07225,0.00000,0.10128,0.06575,0.02721,0.03790,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06823,0.22418,0.04204,0.00000,0.22739,0.09169,0.11924,0.06114,0.09669,0.09800,0.00000,0.07932,0.00000,0.03369,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22992,0.00000,0.12646,0.09902,0.03908,0.25910,0.40553,0.02850,0.03455,0.00000,0.00000,0.03274,0.07032,0.03223,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.03161,0.03847,0.00000,0.06549,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05513,0.11675,0.00000,0.13941,0.00000,0.03426,0.11723,0.00000,0.05111,0.03663,0.16015,0.00000,0.17942,0.19258,0.03035,0.12174,0.00000,0.03716,0.00000,0.02992,0.06957,0.03057,0.18597,0.20792,0.07127,0.00000,0.15990,0.03716,0.02678,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23479,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07695,0.06601,0.02747,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08119,0.03035,0.04014,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('eeb29de245d39f315177e4cfdacb9265ae545bf49f3663b919051f3f1ac879a9', 'General', '', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'DIPANKAR PRAKASH', '20 Sept 2026', 'General Interview Experience', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'Placement Experience

Start sharing your experience...

My placement experience at NIT Jalandhar was a good learning experience. The Training and Placement Cell provided proper guidance and support throughout the placement process. Preparing for aptitude tests, technical rounds, and interviews helped me improve my technical knowledge and communication skills. The support from faculty members and seniors was also very helpful. Overall, the placement journey gave me confidence and valuable exposure for starting my professional career.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16740,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13402,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.43266,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17451,0.00000,0.16375,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07360,0.00000,0.16305,0.00000,0.18063,0.00000,0.00000,0.15209,0.15513,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13007,0.68866,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18155,0.00000,0.00000,0.09446,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14017,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12635,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17045,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('a3173c0f98e9a9b7ba27e625eedea20c3c8f4d4952191135172da72523ca2031', 'Sun', '', '2022-2026', 'IPE', 'VIKASH KUMAWAT', '20 Sept 2026', 'Sun Pharma Selection Experienceere...', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'I am happy to share that I have been selected by Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd. through the campus placement process at NIT Jalandhar.

The selection process included an Online Assessment followed by an interview, covering technical and HR aspects.

The technical discussion focused on my internship, projects, Lean Manufacturing, Quality Control, Supply Chain Management, and Production Engineering concepts. The HR round covered my background, strengths, teamwork, and my motivation to join Sun Pharma.

Overall, it was a great learning experience, and I am grateful to NIT Jalandhar, the TPO team, faculty, seniors, friends, and family for their support.

Looking forward to starting this new journey with Sun Pharma!', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15427,0.20554,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22475,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14867,0.00000,0.00000,0.22251,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16454,0.00000,0.00000,0.19073,0.10767,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14386,0.20464,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.27000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19380,0.00000,0.16903,0.09158,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22475,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19302,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15331,0.00000,0.16185,0.17138,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23508,0.00000,0.00000,0.12564,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12133,0.00000,0.00000,0.17884,0.37555,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23702,0.21209,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('dc5cf7052db3a7bdb0d09cea30a2ba889d6596ae019d1246bcac156b9a4464d2', 'Sunpharma', '', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'HARSIMRANBIR SINGH', '19 Sept 2026', 'Sunpharma placement Experience', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'My placement journey with Sun Pharma was a great learning experience. The recruitment process gave me an opportunity to showcase not only my technical knowledge in Industrial and Production Engineering but also my communication, problem-solving, teamwork, and leadership skills.

I prepared by revising core subjects related to production, quality, manufacturing, and industrial engineering, while also learning about Sun Pharma’s manufacturing processes, values, and work culture. The interview focused on both technical and HR aspects, which helped me understand the importance of connecting academic concepts with practical industrial applications.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15568,0.00000,0.00000,0.13880,0.00000,0.14915,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.35614,0.20104,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13431,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12604,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08550,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20983,0.00000,0.00000,0.17668,0.36041,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20176,0.00000,0.32000,0.00000,0.19106,0.00000,0.00000,0.21421,0.00000,0.14007,0.00000,0.10973,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22908,0.16399,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14678,0.00000,0.15516,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19712,0.00000,0.00000,0.19801,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18093,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16636,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('b8236ea8fb62b65decaf2b702943a4c4573f8e1375232e17d768b43394bb5516', 'Sunpharma', '', '2022-2026', 'MBA', 'PRAKHAR DWIVEDI', '19 Sept 2026', 'Sunpharma Hiring Experience', '{}', '{}', '', 'Happy to share that i got myself placed in Sunpharmaceuticals

My OA got cleared and got into the Interview round,Both the technical and HR round were conducted together

In Technical round i was asked questions related to my Intern and my projects and topics like supply chain management, Lean manufacturing and quality control

In HR round i was asked about my background my overall campus experience ,Why sunpharma ,why pharmaceuticals over FMCG and about my strengths and weaknesses ,Questions regarding company were asked

Overall It was approx 40 min interview and i had to maintain my composure throughout and it all ended well for me

All the best to the one who will be reading this before sitting for the company', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.31182,0.00000,0.16320,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17845,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.33682,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17098,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.50757,0.00000,0.21438,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14543,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16108,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14200,0.00000,0.00000,0.25701,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09975,0.00000,0.16216,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13946,0.00000,0.00000,0.38533,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16840,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17936,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('656d971f8793200a9df9fd8ecf5b035abddd2a603808166a0493bb8f59596163', 'Learning', '', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'ADITYA KUMAR SAH', '19 Sept 2026', 'Learning', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'My placement journey with Silgan Dispensing was a valuable and learning-oriented experience. I was selected for the role of Executive – Operation Excellence at the company’s Dehradun plant.

The selection process helped me understand the importance of both technical knowledge and practical problem-solving skills. My preparation focused on core Industrial & Production Engineering concepts such as Lean Six Sigma, OEE, production planning, process improvement, quality management, data analysis, and manufacturing operations, along with Excel and analytical skills.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22235,0.00000,0.15585,0.00000,0.16747,0.00000,0.00000,0.21933,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19994,0.11287,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15080,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23560,0.00000,0.00000,0.19838,0.40468,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17965,0.00000,0.21452,0.22442,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15728,0.00000,0.24642,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18816,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18747,0.19684,0.00000,0.32961,0.00000,0.17422,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11116,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20315,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('7f60924e52bfc5a8eb4f1d0f01661cf816c0d318ba58b19e297a107b4a337db2', 'General', '', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'MS PRIYANKA SWAMI', '19 Sept 2026', 'General Interview Experience', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'Participated in the campus placement process at Dr. B. R. Ambedkar National Institute of Technology Jalandhar (NIT Jalandhar), gaining valuable exposure to recruitment processes, aptitude assessments, technical interviews, and HR interactions. The experience helped me strengthen my professional communication, interview skills, problem-solving abilities, and understanding of industry expectations.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.28783,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.31058,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23043,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.29757,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.30006,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18656,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.25311,0.00000,0.28035,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23682,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20733,0.00000,0.16242,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.33907,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21725,0.00000,0.22966,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14654,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22292,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('00d6d7a02a6a7d0c4a97f5b5e28e2d62383e0d6e07ca109826ea8fb2a9b46f6b', 'Nitj...', '', '2022-2026', '', 'SURESH PATEL', '19 Sept 2026', 'Placement NITJ...', '{}', '{}', '', 'My placement experience at NIT Jalandhar was honestly not what I had hoped for. I expected a wider range of companies and more opportunities, especially from companies offering roles beyond the core branches. While there were some opportunities available, I felt that the overall placement season could have been much better in terms of the number, variety, and quality of companies visiting the campus. I really wish more reputed companies and diverse roles had been offered, which would have given students a better platform to explore opportunities aligned with their interests and career goals.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.32879,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23370,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15751,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.28936,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23676,0.75211,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.32713,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('810676faae47509a27c66e3acb2e4fa9372302cbafe767602701197974f3be79', 'General', '', '2022-2026', '', 'NAVEEN SINGH', '19 Sept 2026', 'General Interview Experience', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'My placement experience at NIT Jalandhar was very smooth and well organized. The Training and Placement Office (TPO) and the entire placement team provided excellent support throughout the process. From sharing timely information about companies and placement opportunities to coordinating the recruitment process, the TPO made sure that students had the necessary guidance and support at every stage.
The recruitment process helped me understand the importance of preparation, communication skills, technical knowledge, and confidence. The support from the institute and the placement team gave me a positive environment to focus on my preparation and perform my best during the selection process.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11898,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15365,0.00000,0.00000,0.13502,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15493,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06534,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13502,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.61139,0.00000,0.00000,0.30550,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.33546,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.35015,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13398,0.00000,0.11217,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15955,0.00000,0.00000,0.33823,0.07566,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13828,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('f673d7a9bb2a83e391cf3c26e66a53c5131800fc60677721abf34dc84c094244', 'A', '', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'SHAURYA JAISWAL', '19 Sept 2026', 'A Memorable Placement Journey at NIT Jalandhar...', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'My placement journey at NIT Jalandhar was a great learning experience. The process taught me the importance of preparation, patience, and confidence. I am grateful to my institute, faculty, and friends for their constant support. This journey has given me a strong start toward my professional career.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12691,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23316,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.79477,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22752,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.40402,0.00000,0.00000,0.25235,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13855,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('2c210fa9ae4928e07020c7d0479c45cefab28f77191247e62c26ab49c43cbaef', 'Clear', '', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'TEJAL VERMA', '19 Sept 2026', 'Clear Interview Experience', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'I appeared for the HMEL placement process as a Mechanical Engineering student. The selection process consisted of two rounds: one Technical Interview and one HR Interview. The technical round focused mainly on core mechanical engineering concepts and my academic knowledge. The HR round focused on my background, strengths, career goals, and general personality-based questions. I prepared by revising core mechanical subjects and being clear about the concepts mentioned on my resume. Overall, the process was a good learning experience, and I was successfully selected by HMEL. I would recommend candidates to focus on their core technical concepts, revise their resume thoroughly, and stay confident during the interviews.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14110,0.09647,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14628,0.30398,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.30618,0.13251,0.32901,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.26187,0.14783,0.00000,0.00000,0.12991,0.19751,0.00000,0.00000,0.14906,0.00000,0.13987,0.00000,0.00000,0.18535,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18860,0.00000,0.13927,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12991,0.13251,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12743,0.00000,0.00000,0.13198,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11110,0.11765,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15751,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.24206,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07010,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18693,0.00000,0.16657,0.11973,0.00000,0.12277,0.12890,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14494,0.00000,0.00000,0.21839,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('4020ff25590736357374dc328237b8badb6a94189eba7456eb51de9fb44adc93', 'L&T', 'Graduate Engineer Trainee', '2022-2026', 'CE', 'ARCHITA SHARMA', '19 Sept 2026', 'L&T', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'My interview experience with Larsen & Toubro (L&T) for the Graduate Engineer Trainee (GET) role was a good learning experience. The selection process focused on both my technical knowledge and HR round .

During the interview, I was asked questions related to Civil Engineering fundamentals related to subjects like RCC , Concrete Technology , Surveying , academic projects, and practical applications of engineering concepts. There were also questions about my internship experience in technical round . In HR round I was given an extempore topic and was asked to speak on it without prior preparation.

Overall, the interview helped me understand the importance of having strong technical fundamentals, good communication skills, and a willingness to learn. Getting selected as a GET at L&T gave me an opportunity to begin my professional career in a reputed engineering and infrastructure organization.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18706,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11914,0.00000,0.00000,0.10622,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.40882,0.23078,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10278,0.00000,0.22183,0.00000,0.14132,0.29115,0.00000,0.00000,0.19291,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12077,0.19629,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13521,0.13791,0.00000,0.14495,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15440,0.11563,0.00000,0.00000,0.14621,0.15296,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08398,0.00000,0.00000,0.08976,0.00000,0.14592,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.25099,0.00000,0.12824,0.26005,0.00000,0.00000,0.12778,0.13416,0.00000,0.11233,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15085,0.00000,0.00000,0.22730,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13846,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('59cbba11486ee5dfb0f47c2947a47c33a36a2df379e87037f8bb2fc3966a7a00', 'Raik Solutions', '', '2022-2026', '', 'ISHU', '19 Sept 2026', 'RAIK Solutions Interview Experience — 5 Rounds', '{"DSA","DBMS","Operating Systems","OOPs","System Design"}', '{"What problem does the project solve?","What technologies did you use?","Why did you choose those technologies?","How does the application work?"}', '', 'I recently went through the hiring process at RAIK Solutions, which consisted of 5 rounds — 2 assessment rounds, 2 technical interviews, and 1 HR interview.

All rounds were elimination/shortlisting based, so clearing each round was necessary to move forward.

I’ll explain each round and the type of questions I encountered, which may help others preparing for a similar software development role.

Round 1 — Online Assessment

The first round consisted of 30 questions covering a mixture of:

Logical reasoning

Computer Science fundamentals

Technical MCQs

Programming-related concepts

The CS fundamentals included topics such as:

OOPs

DBMS

Operating Systems

Basic programming concepts

Other core CS concepts

The difficulty was moderate, with a combination of conceptual and logical questions.

Round 2 — Technical + Aptitude Assessment

The second round consisted of 13 questions.

The paper included:

10 technical/puzzle-based questions

3 behavioral/writing questions

The technical section tested problem-solving ability and understanding of programming/CS concepts, while the puzzle questions focused more on logical thinking.

The behavioral section was written on paper, where we had to answer questions about ourselves, our approach, and general workplace situations.

This round was slightly different from a typical coding assessment because it tested both technical thinking and behavioral aspects.

Round 3 — Technical Interview

The third round was primarily focused on my projects and technical fundamentals.

The interviewer asked questions related to the projects mentioned on my resume, including:

What problem does the project solve?

What technologies did you use?

Why did you choose those technologies?

How does the application work?

What challenges did you face?

How did you implement particular features?

Apart from projects, I was also asked about:

Basic DSA

SQL

Programming fundamentals

General development concepts

The interview was largely conversational, but knowing your resume and projects thoroughly was important.

Round 4 — Technical Deep Dive

The fourth round was a deeper technical discussion.

The main focus was on:

Projects

Development approach

Technical decision-making

Basic system design

Core programming concepts

The interviewer went deeper into the projects I had previously discussed and asked questions around why I implemented things in a particular way rather than only asking what technologies I used.

Some questions focused on understanding whether I could think beyond simply writing code — for example:

How would you make a feature scalable?

How would you structure the application?

What happens when the number of users/data increases?

How would you improve an existing implementation?

What design choices would you make and why?

This round helped evaluate practical development understanding and problem-solving rather than just theoretical knowledge.

Round 5 — HR Interview

The final round was an HR interview.

The questions were fairly basic and focused on getting to know me better.

Some common areas discussed were:

Tell me about yourself.

Educational background

Projects/internship

Strengths and weaknesses

Career goals

Why do you want to join the company?

General HR/behavioral questions

The conversation was more about personality, communication, career expectations, and overall fit.

Final Takeaway

The RAIK Solutions process was not limited to one particular skill. Across the five rounds, it tested logical reasoning, CS fundamentals, technical knowledge, projects, DSA, SQL, development thinking, system design basics, communication, and behavioral aspects.

My biggest takeaway was:

Don''t prepare only to solve coding questions. Prepare to explain how you build, debug, improve, and scale software.

If you''re preparing for a similar software development role, make sure you can confidently discuss everything written on your resume and understand the fundamentals behind the technologies you''ve used.', '[0.04335,0.00000,0.00000,0.04050,0.07088,0.03977,0.00000,0.04551,0.07498,0.11782,0.03924,0.05366,0.13414,0.22627,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.04270,0.06780,0.06368,0.04050,0.04381,0.17031,0.11056,0.06100,0.00000,0.16993,0.03995,0.04451,0.12039,0.27618,0.18852,0.03824,0.03141,0.04713,0.06081,0.00000,0.02056,0.06683,0.06854,0.03613,0.10987,0.00000,0.17784,0.12437,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10310,0.04358,0.03544,0.07400,0.04381,0.03227,0.10491,0.06389,0.03874,0.00000,0.00000,0.03671,0.03942,0.07226,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18307,0.00000,0.12939,0.00000,0.03671,0.00000,0.00000,0.02927,0.00000,0.03090,0.00000,0.00000,0.03907,0.00000,0.07681,0.00000,0.08626,0.08594,0.00000,0.04488,0.23149,0.02873,0.19190,0.00000,0.27296,0.00000,0.08332,0.00000,0.06707,0.07799,0.06854,0.32430,0.16649,0.03995,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06346,0.08761,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.04742,0.00000,0.24296,0.17710,0.00000,0.12939,0.00000,0.04313,0.03700,0.09240,0.04831,0.08252,0.00000,0.09102,0.03402,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('0a0c07b747883e97734dd0c55d70dcdc59f07ea035045b6084652e3d7a71e59d', 'Blackrock', '', '2022-2026', '', 'MISHTY GUPTA', '19 Sept 2026', 'BlackRock', '{"DSA","DBMS","Operating Systems"}', '{"Is there any project you would like to discuss?","Have you worked in a team?","How did you manage your project as a team?","How did you handle conflicts within the team?"}', '', 'Role: Aladdin Data

Online Assessment (OA)

The OA consisted of:

2 DSA questions — 1 Easy + 1 Advanced

95 MCQs covering: Design Patterns, Cloud Computing, AI, DBMS, Aptitude

Round 1 — Technical + Behavioral

Duration: ~25–30 minutes

The round started with a brief “Introduce yourself” question.

After that, the interviewer asked:

Is there any project you would like to discuss?

Explain your project in detail.

Follow-up and counter questions based on the project.

I discussed one of my projects and was then asked about another project based on GraphRAG. The interviewer specifically asked me to explain GraphRAG as if he had no prior knowledge of it—what it is, why it is used, and what it actually does.

There were multiple counter questions based on my explanation. He also asked whether the project was an individual or team project.

Since I had applied for the Aladdin Data role, my projects were quite relevant to the role and helped me during the discussion.

The interviewer also asked behavioral questions such as:

Have you worked in a team?

How did you manage your project as a team?

How did you handle conflicts within the team?

The round went quite well for me because I had a strong understanding of my projects and was comfortable explaining the technical decisions behind them.

Round 2 — Technical Deep Dive

Duration: ~15–20 minutes

This round was primarily based on my resume and projects.

The interviewer asked me to explain my project and continuously asked counter questions based on whatever I mentioned.

The discussion went quite deep into the technical aspects, including:

Project architecture

Data flow

Technologies and libraries used

How the different components interact

How changes and incremental updates are handled

Which database I used and why I chose it

Why I didn''t use an alternative database

Whether the database supports concurrency and why

What concurrency means

What a deadlock is

Whether I faced any deadlock while working on the project

What an LLM is — “Explain it to a 10-year-old”

What MCP is

What a transaction is in DBMS

Something I was particularly proud of while working on the project

The interviewer kept digging deeper into my answers, so knowing the project beyond just the high-level implementation was very important.

Overall Experience

Both rounds were heavily project-oriented, especially around the projects mentioned on my resume. The interviewers were interested not just in what I had built, but also in why I made certain technical decisions and how the system worked internally.

My biggest takeaway was:

If you mention a project on your resume, be prepared to explain every important technical decision behind it and handle multiple “why?” and “what if?” follow-up questions.

For project-heavy interviews, having a strong understanding of your architecture, data flow, database choices, concurrency, libraries, edge cases, and implementation details can make a big difference.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.05213,0.00000,0.00000,0.05283,0.12521,0.00000,0.23240,0.03913,0.00000,0.17820,0.00000,0.12023,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.04895,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21226,0.11826,0.05330,0.00000,0.12521,0.05080,0.08346,0.00000,0.04039,0.00000,0.02731,0.22195,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11577,0.09416,0.00000,0.05819,0.00000,0.00000,0.21217,0.05145,0.00000,0.00000,0.09752,0.00000,0.04799,0.00000,0.06045,0.05145,0.00000,0.00000,0.05729,0.00000,0.09752,0.10661,0.09071,0.03888,0.00000,0.04105,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05819,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.57253,0.15932,0.04519,0.15540,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10359,0.13657,0.15385,0.04423,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.04955,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.24045,0.16137,0.05881,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08183,0.06418,0.16443,0.00000,0.12090,0.00000,0.11956,0.12090]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('e133121d7a4a2f6ee8c90fe26878cf940b56d6363f05d31bceb5306ad247024f', 'American Express', '', '2021-2025', '', 'VANSHIKA SONI', '18 Sept 2026', 'American Express( Intern + PPO)', '{"DBMS","Operating Systems"}', '{}', 'After my internship, I got PPO. So this was my on campus placement experience. All the best to everyone for placements and wishes great future ahead to everyone ✨️.', 'Last year(2025), I had the opportunity to sit for on campus intern opportunity of Amex. Firstly there was pre placement talk in which focus was on company''s core values, history of Amex and hiring process. After one week, online assessment was scheduled which contained mcqs related to aptitude, machine learning, python and sql.

Around 30 students got selected for the GD round. Two groups with 15 candidates each were divided and given a topic for online group discussion. Around 8 to 10 students were selected for first round of interview.

In first round I was asked several questions on sql, puzzles, guesstimates, how credit card works and general questions related to Amex. 4 students were selected for next round.

Second round was HR + Technical round. Again puzzles, guesstimates and some HR questions were asked. And finally 3 students recieved the offer.

Tips: Research about company before interview. Have a look on interview experiences of different people. Always communicate your thought process to the interviewer properly. Prepare a crisp introduction of yours which include your projects, experience and your interests. And try to end the interview with a relevant question to the interviewer.

After my internship, I got PPO. So this was my on campus placement experience.

All the best to everyone for placements and wishes great future ahead to everyone ✨️.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09949,0.00000,0.00000,0.12506,0.07369,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21472,0.10179,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20263,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07631,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09568,0.07859,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10286,0.00000,0.00000,0.09039,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10372,0.09448,0.00000,0.20357,0.11721,0.12897,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08074,0.17498,0.15985,0.00000,0.09861,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09220,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14646,0.20646,0.00000,0.16372,0.23726,0.00000,0.00000,0.09608,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11229,0.00000,0.00000,0.06001,0.08512,0.14634,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16780,0.00000,0.00000,0.34772,0.00000,0.09994,0.25628,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21920,0.00000,0.42727,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05065,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('5c3c053df0fb2c52952f9f3a399e37671ddef123f47f503bb12cce88ee14844e', 'General', '', '2022-2026', '', 'GURSARANJOT SINGH', '18 Sept 2026', 'General Interview Experience', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'My Placement Experience

My placement journey at NIT Jalandhar was a challenging yet valuable learning experience. During the placement season, I actively participated in the recruitment processes of several companies across core engineering, manufacturing, energy, technology, and other sectors.

I was initially selected by a company through the on-campus placement process. However, before joining, concerns regarding the authenticity and credibility of the opportunity came to light, and the Training and Placement Office advised students not to proceed with the internship opportunity. As a result, I could not consider that opportunity as a genuine career placement.

Although I have not secured an on-campus placement, the experience taught me several important lessons. I participated in aptitude tests, technical assessments, interviews, and HR rounds, which helped me improve my technical preparation, communication skills, confidence, and ability to handle rejection.

I also learned that a successful career is not defined only by campus placement. My internship experience at HMEL, technical projects, leadership experience through the Aeromodelling and Drone Club, and my continued efforts to explore opportunities outside campus have helped me develop practical and professional skills.

Overall, my placement journey has taught me the importance of persistence, self-learning, and taking responsibility for my career. While I would have liked to secure a placement through campus recruitment, I see this experience as an opportunity to continue improving myself and pursue suitable opportunities beyond the campus placement process.', '[0.07896,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07243,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.46892,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05799,0.07376,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05555,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06632,0.26208,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07551,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.04694,0.00000,0.06455,0.00000,0.00000,0.11756,0.03185,0.00000,0.07055,0.00000,0.15631,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13424,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.30059,0.05628,0.65552,0.00000,0.07116,0.07444,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08174,0.00000,0.00000,0.04369,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17065,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06065,0.00000,0.06219,0.00000,0.00000,0.10934,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07776,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11062,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('fcf7fd5a9949fc6044c780f5230c23e6fb22a4e8896eb611283dd0b25ac6b705', 'Cvent', '', '2022-2026', '', 'DANISH BEHAL', '18 Sept 2026', 'Cvent Recruitment (SDE Intern + PPO)', '{"DSA","DBMS","Operating Systems","OOPs"}', '{}', '', 'There were mainly two technical assessments :-

Behavioral + aptitude + OOPS + DBMS + OS :
Behaviroal assessment was done by PI Behavioral Assessment.
Rest of the above mentioned topics were tested through MCQs of easy to medium level. OOPS questions were asked from JAVA. Adequate time was allotted to complete the test.
AI + DSA :
First shortlisting was done based on previous round.
This round consisted of 15 - 20 MCQs based on AI/ML, transformers, training of models.These questions didn''t require memorization of models but conceptual understanding of ML.
The round also consisted of 1 question of DSA - Delete and Earn
45 minutes were given for this round.

After these 20-25 students were selected for interviews:-

Technical Interview I - It was conducted on Zoom and the entire screen was shared. The interviewer asked these questions:
DSA Leetcode Easy - Array question - approach + implementation
DSA Leetcode Medium - Two pointer question - appraoch + implementation
I was asked the time complexity and one test case was run for both of them.
The interviewer himself provided link for a compiler.
I was asked to make a prompt for a chatbot to make some improvements in a code.
One standard GFG puzzle - RaceTracks
REST API - in brief.
API security - how is it done.
Difference between Relational and Non- Relational Databases. When to prefer each.
One question related to project in my resume.
Technical Interview II + HR - It was conducted by one of officials of the company present there at the TPO cell. 2 questions of meduim level leetcode of sliding window were asked (approach + implementation). Then I was asked to make a data structure / class for the scenario given to me. Then a question on as one event in the last one year where I think I could have done better.
Some more HR questions were asked then.

Both these interviews lasted for more than 1 hour each.

Overall the the difficulty level was moderate. The DSA questions were from Striver''s SDE / A2Z sheet.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.15340,0.00000,0.13854,0.07773,0.00000,0.00000,0.34196,0.11514,0.00000,0.10488,0.00000,0.17690,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08345,0.00000,0.00000,0.07915,0.00000,0.00000,0.14406,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07808,0.08700,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.29712,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14763,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10076,0.25552,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06835,0.12488,0.15142,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.26684,0.00000,0.00000,0.06927,0.25290,0.18536,0.07174,0.07843,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06040,0.00000,0.09268,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05616,0.00000,0.33248,0.22865,0.00000,0.00000,0.09157,0.06555,0.05081,0.00000,0.18110,0.00000,0.00000,0.06674,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08345,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11872,0.00000,0.15978,0.08430,0.14702,0.08430,0.00000,0.06020,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('5725b39c705d9a253122d086496404d8449d2a1b40fb233dac1b5a5db8b07441', 'Juspay', '', '2022-2026', 'CSE', 'HARSHITA OBEROI', '18 Sept 2026', 'Getting Selected at Juspay(SDE intern + PPO role)..', '{"DSA","Operating Systems","System Design"}', '{}', '', 'I got selected for Juspay and here’s what the placement process actually looked like. It started with an OA with 3 questions mainly based on Graphs DP and Trees. Then came a pen and paper MCQ round covering CS fundamentals Physics and Maths.

After that was the Hackathon Part A and Part B. Hackathon A was mainly about solving the Tree of Space problem and getting the implementation right. Hackathon B was around 7 hours long. It focused on optimizing the solution and figuring out better approaches along with their time complexities and deriving the complexity of the optimized approaches. There were also questions around OS Networking and other CS fundamentals.

Then came the interviews. They were conducted in person in Bengaluru and the technical round was around 1 to 1.5 hours. It went deep into DSA especially Graphs and DP. They kept pushing on the approach and asked why it works and whether it can be optimized and what the complexity would be along with edge cases. Then came LLD and System Design where I was asked to design something around BookMyShow. There were also basic maths questions followed by a proper resume deep dive. Basically anything you put on your resume was fair game. Skills projects and technologies could be picked up and drilled into. Then came questions around OS and even CPU microarchitecture.

After around 1 to 1.5 hours of technical questioning there was another 30 minute HR round.

Small tip: It’s not just about getting the answer. Make the interviewer understand how you think. Explain your approach step by step. Talk through your assumptions and why you are choosing a particular solution. If you see a better approach then say it. Even when you are stuck keep communicating your thought process. Sometimes how clearly you explain your thinking matters just as much as the final answer. 😄', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23528,0.30886,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14521,0.00000,0.00000,0.07794,0.09742,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12931,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.24682,0.00000,0.00000,0.23314,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08832,0.00000,0.00000,0.19415,0.09955,0.00000,0.07979,0.11350,0.17220,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11819,0.00000,0.07488,0.12659,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09280,0.11252,0.00000,0.00000,0.21326,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11252,0.00000,0.20591,0.12529,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09919,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09505,0.13775,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08321,0.00000,0.13038,0.00000,0.00000,0.06968,0.00000,0.22655,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15103,0.09955,0.20187,0.00000,0.00000,0.19838,0.00000,0.00000,0.08720,0.27057,0.09218,0.00000,0.10836,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11763,0.12861,0.00000,0.00000,0.10925,0.00000,0.10749,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13220,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('29cc9533f891aef7d8053ec2fbf10f9175c3c4fcb527490455a3627be4133cc5', 'ENTNT', '', '2022-2026', 'CSE', 'VANSH MAURYA', '18 Sept 2026', 'Entnt Hiring Process', '{"DBMS","Operating Systems","OOPs"}', '{}', '', 'Note: All the 4 rounds(2 Online Assessments and 2 Technical Interviews) are shortlisting based elimination rounds.

The first 2 rounds were pretty easy to clear so I will be focussing on the interview rounds in this article.

OA 1:- Algorithm Coding questions in JavaScript (Very basic questions). MCQs on CS Fundamentals[OOPS, OS, DBMS]. Format of the questions - Video on questions to expect in the first round.

OA 2:- Coding questions on SQL (All from Leetcode). Output based MCQs on JavaScript. CS fundamentals[OOPS, OS, DBMS]. Similar to OA1

with a slight more difficulty level.

Technical Interview 1:- This round was a heavy resume based round and primarily evaluated javascript knowledge via output based questions. Difficulty in this round can vary from person to person [Check My profile here] , for me personally, they asked about the remote internship I worked for 6 months, my role there, the products/features I built (not in depth due to NDA, just how a general product/feature like that is made). Focussed on web development approach and style, react + node.js, RAG and mobile app development (purely due to my resume).

Spent around 10 minutes discussing theoretical Operating Systems and OOPs in Java.

Then finally before ending the meeting asked me to approach designing a database (no right or wrong answers), it was a library management system where a Student can issue a Book, a Book can have multiple Copies and these Copies can be on different LibraryShelfs.

Technical Interview 2:- This round primarily focus on you development skills. Focus was on how you approach a real-world problem while working on a codebase, mainly senario based questions and design based questions.

Here are some of the questions (only the ones I can remember)-

Question1- The dev before you wrote a particular code for an admin dashboard, find the mistake in it and tell us how you''d improve it. The dashboard rendered 50 items at once in a react component. It worked well in development/testing but breaks in production.

Question 2- There 4 small tables for an inventory management system was given. My task was to indentify PK and FKs in them.

Question 3- Hands-on live coding in React. For the given flat list,

comments = [

{

id: ''...'',

parentId: ''...'',

heading: ''...'',

description: ''...''

},

...];

render it in a tree like structure,

ParentComment

|-- ChildComment

|-- |-- GrandChildComment

... and so on.

The depth of the tree is not restricted, can be upto any limit.

Question 4- Design database for an inventory management system considering a User can place multiple Orders, there are several Products the user can choose to directly buy or buy through cart. (Only database design and reason for those design choices, how those choices will make it able to make the code scalable and production safe).

Question 5- In a React code, the dashboard page is taking a lot of time to load, this problem only occurs in production not in local development testing. Identify how you would debug this problem, what main issues would you first look for in the code-base, how you aim to improve the quality now. (Give answer from Front-end, Back-end and DB side perspective).

How to prepare -

Learn CS fundamentals well.
Actively make hands-on projects with least AI assistance.
Learn just not to code but also to build and ship an optimised product.', '[0.00000,0.07015,0.06284,0.06485,0.17025,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08004,0.00000,0.00000,0.25777,0.05370,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06769,0.00000,0.34183,0.16284,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20407,0.00000,0.14255,0.25702,0.36853,0.00000,0.06124,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11571,0.00000,0.00000,0.14238,0.06638,0.12094,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05168,0.08399,0.00000,0.06202,0.00000,0.00000,0.11755,0.00000,0.05785,0.00000,0.07287,0.12405,0.00000,0.05675,0.20719,0.00000,0.00000,0.06426,0.10935,0.04687,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06150,0.00000,0.00000,0.13761,0.00000,0.03593,0.00000,0.00000,0.03841,0.21791,0.28098,0.06485,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08325,0.05488,0.18546,0.21328,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.04806,0.00000,0.00000,0.07015,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07593,0.00000,0.09726,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06022,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14412,0.07287]');
