The interview primarily focused on my resume. Since I had already worked in ad tech, they asked me about terms like CTR, CPI, and other related concepts. They also asked about all my past experiences. There were also some case studies that focused on general business scenarios, such as, “Revenue has dropped. How would you identify the reason?” The rest of the interview focused on why I was a good candidate for the role.

For these types of interviews, I suggest properly revising your resume and learning a bit about what the company does so that you understand the business. Apart from that, focus on your skills and prepare around the experience mentioned on your resume.

For case studies, I suggest doing mock practice with someone. Interviewers also usually ask if you have any questions for them, so prepare a few questions before the interview. This can leave a really good impression.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18307,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14831,0.00000,0.10396,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15057,0.00000,0.00000,0.13232,0.30177,0.00000,0.00000,0.30367,0.00000,0.28495,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.25615,0.00000,0.14186,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13497,0.00000,0.14186,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13443,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.28131,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14281,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12282,0.28561,0.12551,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10993,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13551,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.49445,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('33b257cdc521e5f25cc44b27c149a131f96ba67fe07d3bfc58e8b4573145b4ba', 'NXP', '', '2022-2026', 'VLSI', 'LAKSHYA KUMAR SHARMA', '17 Sept 2026', 'NXP Semiconductors', '{"Core Electronics"}', '{}', '', 'Hiring was for the functional safety role. There were two rounds of interview. First one was technical and second was HR follow up round.

In first round , Interviewer asked majorly on the projects and VLSI design concept along with Digital IC design,STA, FSMs. Discussed about pre layout and post layout analysis in physical design as reference from my project .In the end he asked about vlsi testing part. During the whole interview he was mainly questioning on the projects in my resume.

In the follow up round, interviewer asked me about myself and family. She asked me about the NXP, work culture and opportunity at NXP ,my future goals after some years, Academics and the competitive exams i gave.

Thankyou', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.45875,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.55240,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11827,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16046,0.29317,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16262,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18933,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13185,0.22014,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11928,0.15725,0.31888,0.15279,0.18330,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09290,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15611,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('09851d887e5ee9b97e566b1ddff2a83a83b8c60c24fec880b222096d16e925b2', 'UKG', '', '2022-2026', '', 'HERMAN KAUR', '17 Sept 2026', 'My Placement Experience at UKG', '{"DSA","Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'Getting placed at UKG was a valuable and enriching experience. The selection process consisted of multiple rounds designed to evaluate technical knowledge, problem-solving ability, AI understanding, communication skills, and overall personality.

1. Online Assessment

The first round was an online assessment consisting of two questions:

DSA Problem: A data structures and algorithms-based coding problem was given to assess problem-solving and coding skills.
Debugging Problem: The second question involved a folder containing multiple files of an existing project. We were given the flexibility to choose a preferred technology/tech stack and were required to analyze the project, identify the issues or errors, and debug the code accordingly.
2. Technical Interview

The second stage was a virtual technical interview, which lasted approximately 30–40 minutes.

The interview covered:

Discussion about the projects I had worked on, including my contributions and the technologies used.
Questions related to Computer Science fundamentals, including core concepts.
A medium-level DSA problem, where I was asked to explain my approach and arrive at a solution.
Follow-up questions based on my projects and technical knowledge.
3. AI Assessment Round

The third stage was an in-person AI assessment, lasting approximately 1 hour.

In this round:

I was given a problem statement and asked to develop appropriate prompts to solve the given problem.
I had to explain the reasoning behind my prompts and how I would improve them.
The interviewer asked questions about prompt engineering and AI concepts.
There was also a discussion around my AI-related projects and the approaches I had used.
The round involved considerable questioning, reasoning, and iteration, which tested my ability to think critically and communicate my approach.
4. HR Interview

The final stage was an HR interview, which lasted around 10–15 minutes.

The discussion focused more on my personality and background. Some of the areas covered were:

Introduction and questions about myself and my background.
My inspirations and career goals.
Questions about my family and hobbies.
Questions related to leadership, teamwork, and handling responsibilities.
General questions to understand my personality and interests beyond academics.', '[0.14709,0.00000,0.33287,0.00000,0.12025,0.00000,0.00000,0.07720,0.12720,0.19987,0.13315,0.09103,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07243,0.11501,0.05401,0.00000,0.07432,0.09631,0.06252,0.05174,0.14414,0.00000,0.06777,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15988,0.00000,0.10316,0.06178,0.06975,0.11338,0.05814,0.00000,0.04659,0.00000,0.05028,0.07033,0.25627,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08745,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.14863,0.00000,0.14831,0.05419,0.00000,0.06687,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12259,0.00000,0.07720,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08044,0.00000,0.13615,0.00000,0.09931,0.00000,0.05242,0.05551,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.38877,0.00000,0.03807,0.00000,0.09749,0.12208,0.05772,0.26461,0.00000,0.14134,0.00000,0.17068,0.00000,0.00000,0.15719,0.05649,0.13554,0.00000,0.06082,0.00000,0.10184,0.07900,0.10766,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13739,0.07511,0.00000,0.07317,0.00000,0.00000,0.06277,0.05225,0.00000,0.13999,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07634,0.00000]');
