HR Questions', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.29203,0.00000,0.00000,0.14797,0.00000,0.00000,0.09300,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11349,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16563,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.45250,0.13550,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09590,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13012,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13187,0.00000,0.17643,0.00000,0.00000,0.25410,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.37976,0.43527,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.34476,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17029,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('5153502bd292f529e7726de831ab9bcb6f1d03e770d2a4f54d925e078bda1e86', 'Zscaler', '', '2021-2025', '', 'TANIYA', '17 Sept 2026', 'Zscaler', '{"DSA","DBMS","Operating Systems","OOPs"}', '{"Online Assessment (OA)","Project + Resume-Based Interview","HR/Behavioral Interview"}', '', 'I was selected for a two-month Software Development Internship at Zscaler through the campus placement process, which was conducted in September 2025. The internship was scheduled from 8 June to 8 August 2026, and based on my performance during the internship, I was subsequently converted to a Full-Time Employment (FTE) offer.

Selection Process

The selection process consisted of an Online Assessment followed by three interview rounds.

1. Online Assessment (OA)
The OA primarily tested basic Computer Science fundamentals through MCQs, along with programming skills. It included:

CS fundamentals and basic technical MCQs

One Data Structures coding question in a language of the candidate''s choice

One Python-based MCQ/question

2. Technical Interview
The first interview was primarily focused on Data Structures and CS fundamentals. I was asked two Data Structures problems, followed by questions covering core CS subjects. The discussion particularly included:

C programming and fundamental concepts

DBMS

Object-Oriented Programming (OOPs) principles

The round involved both problem-solving and conceptual questions, so having a strong understanding of fundamental concepts was important.

3. Project + Resume-Based Interview
The second round focused mainly on my resume, projects, technical experience, and co-curricular activities. The interviewer went through my resume in detail and asked questions about the projects and technologies mentioned in it. I was also asked to explain my co-curricular activities, roles, responsibilities, and involvement in various college activities. I was expected to clearly explain my contributions and experiences mentioned on my resume.

4. HR/Behavioral Interview
The final round focused on HR and behavioral questions. The discussion covered general behavioral situations, experiences, and questions aimed at understanding my approach to different situations.

During the two-month internship, we had regular demos and review meetings with our mentors and managers. These sessions were an important part of the evaluation process. We were expected to present our work, explain the approach we had taken, discuss the challenges we faced, and demonstrate our progress. Based on my overall performance during the two-month internship, I received a PPO for Full-Time Employment (FTE) at Zscaler.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12954,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13703,0.10765,0.00000,0.19613,0.12257,0.24810,0.07842,0.00000,0.00000,0.08135,0.00000,0.06195,0.00000,0.00000,0.08006,0.10375,0.06735,0.05574,0.07764,0.23291,0.21901,0.08135,0.00000,0.08412,0.00000,0.06989,0.11482,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.03757,0.18321,0.06263,0.00000,0.15058,0.14281,0.16250,0.07577,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09421,0.00000,0.12954,0.13524,0.00000,0.29490,0.15977,0.05838,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06477,0.00000,0.00000,0.13416,0.00000,0.12480,0.10699,0.00000,0.05647,0.05980,0.08666,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05235,0.07505,0.16405,0.25383,0.05251,0.08767,0.12435,0.17816,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19003,0.00000,0.12700,0.06085,0.07300,0.06240,0.13104,0.00000,0.05486,0.00000,0.05799,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07367,0.00000,0.00000,0.11100,0.08091,0.00000,0.07882,0.13746,0.00000,0.00000,0.11258,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08317,0.06218,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('732febd2a05f4ebfb73cdcff3757d7705eaaa551b12cd786cd40958ea328b40a', 'Mondelez International', '', '2022-2026', 'IT', 'RHYTHEM', '17 Sept 2026', 'Mondelez International', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'I joined Mondelēz International through the on-campus summer internship process and later converted it into a Pre-Placement Offer (PPO) following the mid-term and final project reviews. If you are preparing for Mondelēz, here is the honest truth about what the team actually looks for and how the process works.

The Biggest Myth: Branch Preference

There is a common misconception on campus that Mondelēz only looks for IPE students. That is completely untrue. Every eligible branch has an equal shot. What actually differentiates candidates isn’t your department name on paper—it’s ownership and your practical, problem-solving mindset.

Shortlisting Criteria

Strict 8.0+ CGPA: Keep your grades up. They adhere strictly to the cutoff for initial shortlisting.

Round 1: The Group Discussion (Data & Case-Based)

The GD isn’t a generic debate on current affairs. They hand you a real, operational case study packed with numbers.

The Reality: Analyzing the numbers matters, but your assertiveness and communication carry far more weight. Honestly, the panel isn’t just looking for textbook correct math; they want to see who can command the room, speak with calm confidence, and drive the discussion without getting flustered. Make your presence felt early and hold your ground.

Round 2: Personal Interview (~30 to 35 Minutes)

Coursework over Academic Projects: The interviewers focused much more on core engineering and supply chain coursework rather than standard academic projects.

Resume Strategy: If you have coding or software projects, tone them down. Unless you applied programming directly to solve an industrial or automation problem, Mondelēz is interested in manufacturing, logistics, and process efficiency. Reframe any technical work around automation and business impact.

Case Studies & Mindset: Expect scenarios centered around inventory management, bottlenecks, and supply chain trade-offs. If you understand Lean Six Sigma and can frame your answers using structured root-cause thinking, you will immediately stand out.

Prior Internships Matter: They will grill you thoroughly on past hands-on training or internship experience. You must know your numbers, your exact contribution, and why you took every single decision.

Converting the Internship into a PPO

The internship itself is all about execution. Treat your project like you own the facility: identify gaps, apply continuous improvement tools, stay proactive on the shop floor, and communicate your deliverables clearly to the mentors. Complete ownership of your project from day one is what seals the PPO.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07992,0.00000,0.00000,0.25564,0.12119,0.00000,0.13259,0.00000,0.10098,0.09484,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09086,0.00000,0.00000,0.11899,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18715,0.00000,0.00000,0.10847,0.06123,0.00000,0.10208,0.00000,0.08181,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13955,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.38453,0.05208,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10934,0.11741,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11538,0.00000,0.00000,0.12847,0.00000,0.00000,0.11953,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09747,0.42373,0.11638,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.12847,0.17066,0.00000,0.20054,0.13791,0.25677,0.21435,0.00000,0.00000,0.12063,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07743,0.00000,0.13800,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09452,0.00000,0.00000,0.12718,0.00000,0.00000,0.13480,0.06031,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11022,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.13633,0.00000,0.10134,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('43e179204863c60318a2eff96e2f726250f666e7ccb5cae6adf40aed1aabe67f', 'Jubilant', '', '2022-2026', 'IT', 'VINEET CHHABRA', '17 Sept 2026', 'Experience at Jubilant Ingrevia', '{"Operating Systems","Core Mechanical","Core Chemical"}', '{}', '', 'It was smooth and comfortable experience. For summer internship, it is a three step process : online assessment, Group discussion and personal interview. Knowledge about core concepts of chemical engineering is necessary like heat transfer, mass transfer, fluid mechanics etc.

The experience at the site was welcoming and filled with practical knowledge about process engineering and safety practices.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17807,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17161,0.00000,0.18440,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18992,0.00000,0.00000,0.44031,0.37284,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.28322,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19511,0.10571,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.43687,0.00000,0.00000,0.23418,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17696,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.23621,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.27134,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('ed725cbc9ecbe78b7df016a45b4df81e8d6bf15da5d3f132f3e21b037ce65441', 'Mondelez International', '', '2022-2026', '', 'LATA GUPTA', '17 Sept 2026', 'Mondelez International Interview Experience', '{}', '{"Group Discussion (GD) – 15–20 Minutes","Personal Interview – 40–45 Minutes"}', '', '1. Group Discussion (GD) – 15–20 Minutes

The GD round lasted around 15–20 minutes. We were given a supply-related case study and approximately 2 minutes to read and understand the case before the discussion started.

The case required us to analyse the situation, identify the key problem, and discuss possible solutions from a practical business and supply-chain perspective.

The panel mainly observed communication, logical thinking, problem-solving, teamwork, listening skills, and how we handled different opinions. The focus was not on speaking continuously but on making relevant points and contributing meaningfully to the discussion.

2. Personal Interview – 40–45 Minutes

The personal interview lasted around 40–45 minutes, with the main focus on the resume.

They went through the resume in detail and asked questions from internships, projects, and core subjects. For core subjects, it is better to prepare at least 2–3 subjects in depth. The questions were not limited to definitions; they focused more on practical applications, real-life scenarios, and how the concepts are used in industry.

Internships and projects should be prepared very thoroughly. Be clear about what you did, why you did it, your individual contribution, challenges faced, and what you learned. They can ask follow-up questions to check whether you genuinely understand the work mentioned on your resume.

Basic supply-chain concepts should also be prepared, especially for an operations/supply-chain-oriented role. The interviewer may connect your technical knowledge and internship experience with practical industrial situations.

Along with technical and resume-based questions, they also asked HR questions to understand my motivation, experiences, teamwork, and overall personality.

Overall Takeaway

The most important thing is to prepare your resume thoroughly. If you have mentioned an internship, project, or technical subject, be ready for detailed questions and practical applications. For core subjects, prepare 2–3 subjects deeply rather than trying to memorise definitions from many subjects. Also, have a good understanding of basic supply-chain concepts and common HR questions

Start sharing your experience...', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.09100,0.00000,0.00000,0.04884,0.12210,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.07696,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05796,0.00000,0.00000,0.15503,0.00000,0.16658,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17160,0.06962,0.17157,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11227,0.00000,0.00000,0.13155,0.05000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06875,0.07082,0.00000,0.08529,0.09385,0.00000,0.06452,0.00000,0.00000,0.11751,0.09549,0.05816,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.06578,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.08332,0.06452,0.00000,0.00000,0.13365,0.36527,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.11251,0.00000,0.00000,0.28452,0.00000,0.20975,0.15950,0.00000,0.10430,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05231,0.08734,0.00000,0.24846,0.07372,0.00000,0.00000,0.06105,0.23662,0.06239,0.04217,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.05465,0.00000,0.05777,0.00000,0.06791,0.00000,0.44032,0.00000,0.00000,0.11058,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.20208,0.05607,0.00000,0.07512,0.00000,0.08285,0.06194,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('a793720a3d2d2166ab74e1118d199068ece18660fa3e82d5efa49bf52c5163db', 'Exl', 'Associate Consultant', '2022-2026', 'ME', 'RHYTHM GABA', '17 Sept 2026', 'My Placement Journey at EXL', '{"Operating Systems"}', '{}', '', 'I was placed as a Business Analyst – Band A2 at EXL through the campus placement process. The selection process was a good learning experience and involved multiple rounds that tested my analytical, technical, problem-solving, and communication skills. Preparing for the process helped me strengthen my fundamentals and build more confidence in approaching different types of problems. Overall, the experience was smooth and rewarding, and getting placed at EXL has been a great start to my professional journey.', '[0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22062,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.16369,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.19661,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.21138,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15238,0.00000,0.00000,0.20001,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.44123,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.18947,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.15887,0.33645,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.22174,0.14727,0.21113,0.34613,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.17120,0.00000,0.00000,0.18432,0.00000,0.15432,0.00000,0.16314,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.10409,0.00000,0.00000,0.22174,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000,0.00000]');
INSERT INTO interview_experiences_pgvector (experience_id, company_name, role, batch, branch, author, date, title, technical_topics, key_questions, preparation_tips, full_text, embedding) VALUES ('4784a964a1787308d48f33139a3425cb10e345070e194ae400c0cd64ae5bb934', 'Kuantum Papers', 'Operations Manager', '2022-2026', '', 'DIVYANSHU KUMAR', '17 Sept 2026', 'Kuantum Papers Interview Experience', '{}', '{}', '', 'My placement experience at Kuantum Papers was not as enriching as I had initially expected. Although I got the opportunity to work in the Environment/ETP department and gained practical exposure to wastewater treatment, BOD, COD, TSS, ETP operations, breakdown monitoring, and plant parameters, the overall work environment and learning experience were somewhat limited.

